'''Ushar''' was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Databank" /> [[humanoid]] [[Force-sensitive]] who served as a member of the [[Knights of Ren]], under the command of an individual known as [[Ren (human)|Ren]].<ref name="The Rise of Kylo Ren 1" /> Ushar and the other Knights later accepted [[Ben Solo]], who took on the name "Kylo Ren," as their new [[Ren|leader]].<ref name="The Rise of Kylo Ren 4">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 4|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 4]]</ref> Kylo went on to join the [[First Order]], ultimately becoming its [[Supreme Leader]], before being redeemed to the [[light side of the Force]]. Now Ben Solo once again, the former Knight killed Ushar and the other Knights on [[Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Biography==
A short time after the hunt for [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], Ushar and the other [[Knights of Ren]] were lurking in the [[Sith Citadel]] of [[Darth Sidious]] on [[Exegol]]. During the [[battle of Exegol]], [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], now the redeemed Ben Solo, entered the Citadel to save Rey.<ref name="Episode IX" />

[[File:KyloFacesTheKnightsOfRen.png|thumb|left|250px|The redeemed Ben Solo faced his former allies on Exegol.]]
Before Solo could reach the [[Throne of the Sith]], Ushar and the Knights confronted their former leader.<ref name="Episode IX" /> Solo briefly thought that the Knights were going to help him, but their hate towards him made Solo realize they had always been loyal to Sidious.<ref name="TROS Expanded Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> The Knights were able to swiftly overwhelm Solo in his unarmed state, forcing him to the ground and beating him. However, through the use of their [[Force-bond]], Rey was able to give Solo his [[Skywalker lightsaber|grandfather's lightsaber]]. With [[Anakin Skywalker|Anakin's]] lightsaber, Ben swiftly cut down [[Kuruk]] and [[Cardo]] before [[Force push]]ing [[Ap'lek]] into a pit, and then cutting [[Vicrul]] down. [[Trudgen]] tried attacking their former leader but was effortlessly killed by Solo. As the last Knight, Ushar tried attacking as well but the redeemed [[Jedi]] leapt over him and stabbed him through the back.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Ushar-CEUEEd.png|thumb|right|250px|Ushar wielded a war club as his preferred weapon.]]
{{Quote|Take him! He's only one man!|Ushar underestimating the power of [[Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="The Rise of Kylo Ren 2">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 2|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 2]]</ref>}}
Ushar was the most likely of the Knights to force prisoners to beg for mercy. He enjoyed testing the mettle of his victims. Ushar believed that ones who whimpered deserved a slow punishment while those who fought back were lauded and earned his personal respect as well as a quick death.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Powers and abilities==
Ushar was [[Force-sensitive]] and an adept with the [[dark side of the Force]] but he was untrained which made his powers stunted.

Despite his great skill as a Knight of Ren, Ushar was quickly killed from a stab from the back by his redeemed former [[Ren|Master]], Ben Solo during the battle of Exegol.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Equipment==
[[File:UsharsWarClub-TROSSeries2Weapons.png|thumb|left|250px|Ushar wielded a vibroblade as a secondary weapon.]]
Ushar's [[Ushar's war club|weapon of choice]] was a [[war club]] with a blunt heavy end. On the end of his war club was a [[kinetite generator]] charged end with concussion vector vanes that would release a widely dispersed concussive blast when a target was hit. Ushar had a [[Vibro-machete|vibromachete]] in an inverted [[sheath]] on his torso. Ushar also made use of shaped baradium charges that made devastating area effect weapons.<ref name="TROS VD" />

Like the rest of the Knights of Ren, Ushar wore all black clothing. He wore [[Ironweave|iron weave]] [[vambrace]]s that allowed him to perform a crushing backhand. Ushar wore a [[helmet]] with [[breathing tube]]s and anti-ox filters which could suggest that it originated from a non-human. His helmet was partially crumpled from a previous attack by a particularly feisty prisoner.<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Knights-of-Ren-concept-art.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Concept art of Ushar by Glyn Dillon.]]
Ushar first appeared in a Force vision in the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], the first installment in the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[sequel trilogy]].<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> In the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], Ushar was portrayed by martial artist [[Ashley Beck]], although the character was only listed as "Knight of Ren" in the film's credits.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|AshBeckStuntsUK|status/1207994596309045255|[[Ashley Beck]]|quote=It was awesome playing a "Knights of Ren" in the new StarWars: The Rise of Skywalker! Massive thanks to @badmonk_uk and @[[Wikipedia:Eunice Huthart|eunicehuv]] for the amazing opportunity!|archiveurl=https://archive.is/EX218}}</ref> The character was simultaneously identified in ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'', ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Galactic Guide]]'', and his card in [[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]], all of which were released in tandem with the movie.<ref name="TROS VD" /><ref name="EpIXGG">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Galactic Guide]]''</ref><ref name="Card Trader">[[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]]</ref>

The design for Ushar was created by artist [[Glyn Dillon]] for ''The Force Awakens''. Like the other Knights, Ushar's design was based off of unused concept art for the "Jedi Killer", a character that eventually evolved into Kylo Ren. Dillon referred to Vicrul's design as "x head" in ''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''.<ref name="Force Awakens Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref>

